  encoding check: Thai present and well formed (no mojibake); 1,045 rows carry Thai script.
  no optional legal-entity or legal-entity-country column present; those feed fields stay empty.

LEXICON
  Appendix A of spec.md parsed as the authority: 14 categories, 286 distinct keywords
  (291 per-tab entries, 5 cross-tab collisions resolved per 2.4 plus 1 within-Casino duplicate).

WORKING SET (spec 3)
  22,032 rows dropped as Review needed; 37 duplicate URLs dropped. standard total = 31,798.
  status normalisation: Illegal gambling -> Gambling (9,175 after de-duplication);
  Scraping url -> Unknown (11,001); Licensed gambling rows in input = 0.

ASSIGNMENT (spec 4)
  keyword-assigned 338, inferred 8,837. inferredShare 96.3%, generalShare 15.7%.
  inferredShare exceeds the 30% threshold in 4.6, so the report states plainly that lexicon
  coverage of this dataset is poor and that subcategory figures are indicative only. Cause is
  structural: the lexicon is predominantly Thai while only 666 of 9,175 gambling rows carry Thai
  script in their description text.
  abbreviation watch (2.3): PG accounts for 99 of 137 abbreviation matches (72.3%), above the 20%
  threshold, and is flagged in the report footnote.

CLUSTERING (spec 5)
  5.2 rule 1 applied as written: a Variant/Redirect row with a seed takes stem(seed) as its cluster
  key. An earlier implementation merged the row's own stem group with the seed's group, which is
  transitive and collapsed 30,198 of 31,798 URLs into one degenerate cluster. Reverted to the
  literal rule.
  5.2 rule 3 near-miss merge is pairwise and non-transitive: only an unmerged representative may
  absorb another unmerged key, so a>ab>abc cannot chain past the 0.90 floor. Stems under 3
  characters and all-numeric stems are excluded from acting as a merge hub.
  thresholds: Jaro-Winkler 0.90, minimum stem length 3, minimum common prefix 4. All are recorded
  in the report footnote as 9.1 requires.
  result: 2,491 clusters, 1,342 multi-URL, 1,149 singletons, clustersToHalf 78.

CARD B1
  236 gambling rows carry a numeric rank. 26 passed the Thai-audience test on description text
  alone with no Vietnamese-audience indicator; the ten best ranked are rendered.
  0 otherwise eligible ranked rows were excluded on a Vietnamese indicator, so that line is omitted.
  (2,644 gambling rows overall carry a Vietnamese indicator, but none of them is both ranked and
  Thai-evidenced.)

OMISSIONS, EACH BECAUSE THE INPUT DOES NOT CARRY THE VALUE
